<p class="country-intro">Japan is an island nation of over 6,800 islands, blending ancient temples and traditions with some of the world&#39;s most advanced technology. Japan is located in Eastern Asia and has a population of around 123.2 million. Its capital city is Tokyo, and the most widely spoken official language is Japanese. As an island nation, Japan has no land borders.</p>
<p>By the numbers, Japan is the 11th most populous of the 196 countries covered on this site, home to 1.54% of the world&#39;s population. By land area it ranks 62nd out of 196, with a population density of roughly 326 people per km².</p>
<p class="last-verified">Facts last checked 16 September 2026.</p>

